# <type>(<scope>): <summary>
#
# ── Subject ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# type:    feat fix docs test refactor perf chore ci build revert
# scope:   a crate without the postio- prefix (gtk, storage, ui, ...),
#          a top-level directory (scripts, macos, specs, docs, ...), or
#          workspace tooling ci deps release hooks skills checks land
#          claim; several joined by commas: (ui,gtk)
# summary: imperative mood, no trailing period, <= 50 chars
#          "add draft autosave"  not  "Added draft autosave."
#
# ── Body (optional, wrap at 72) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Explain WHY, not what — the diff already says what. Worth writing when
# the change encodes a decision, a trade-off, or a non-obvious constraint.
#
# ── Footer ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Refs: #123                  (on an issue branch; none on fix/ docs/ chore/)
# Refs: specs/011-contacts T004   (on a feature/ branch)
#
# Never a closing keyword (close, fix, resolve + #N), not even negated:
# GitHub closes #N when the squash lands. Write "leaves #N open". The
# PR's Closes line does the closing.
#
# .githooks/commit-msg (scripts/commit-msg.py) refuses what breaks these.
